.TH PUBLISH-SITE 1 "October 2026" "Noble Factor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Publish-Site \- build the DevLore site and publish it to production, prompting for an Azure login
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Publish-Site
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Publish-Site
checks the Azure login and opens a browser to log in when there is none, shows the subscription and user,
installs the site's dependencies with
.BR "npm ci" ,
builds it, reads the Static Web App's deployment token with
.BR "az staticwebapp secrets list" ,
installs the SWA CLI when it is missing, and deploys
.I dist
to the production environment with that token.
The app is devlore-noblefactor-com in rg-devlore-site.
It runs from the repository's root, wherever it is called from.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this manual page and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success \- the site is published.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error \- a missing or invalid option.
.TP
.B 69
A tool it needs is not on PATH, or the deployment token cannot be read: the Static Web App does not exist or the login cannot see it.
.TP
.B 72
Critical file missing \- \fBDeclare-BashScript\fR is not on PATH; deploy the base layer, NobleFactor/noblefactor-engprod.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bin/Publish-Site
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR Deploy-Site (1),
.BR az (1)
